OL,3,GNEWSABus travel is changing in the West
OL,4,AMidlands - what will it mean for you?
OL,5,
OL,6,FBus services in the West Midlands
OL,7,Fconurbation are to be brought back into
OL,8,Fpublic control for the first time in 40
OL,9,Fyears.
OL,11,FPrime Minister Andy Burnham was in
OL,12,FWolverhampton to make the announcement
OL,13,Fand backed what he called a "bold move"
OL,14,Fand the "biggest act of public control"
OL,15,Fsince he came into office.
OL,17,FThe West Midlands bus deal would
OL,18,Fprotect thousands of jobs, Mr Burnham
OL,19,Fsaid, after they were threatened after
OL,20,Fthe parent company behind local
OL,21,Foperator National Express indicated it
OL,22,Fwas leaving the market.
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,355,350,200,160,0,100
